7. The points that arise for my consideration are;
1. Whether the petitioner prove that petitioner has been subjected to cruelty of domestic violence and neglected by the respondents?
2. Whether the petitioner further prove that, the respondents having sufficient means and has deserted the petitioner?
3. Whether the petitioner is entitled for maintenance?
4. What order?
8. The findings of this Court on the above points are as under:
 Point No.1 : In the Affirmative;
 Point No.2 : In the Affirmative;
 Crl.Mis.No.113/2017  JUDGMENT  Point No.3 : In the Partly Affirmative;
 Point No.4 : As per final order for the  following:
 REASONS 9. Points No.1 & 2: Since these points are interrelated, they have been grouped together for discussion for the sake of convenience and to avoid repetition of facts and evidence.
10. It is specific case of the petitioner that, petitioner being legally wedded wife of respondent No.1 has been subjected to cruelty and domestic violence by the respondents.

